            {
              "id": "3075a26d-1b2f-3587-aaa1-113f4b7a4e5a",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\n\"Unsecured Web Address\" vulnerability refers to the use of unencrypted HTTP protocol to access or transfer data over the internet. This can lead to potential security risks such as Man-in-the-Middle (MitM) attacks, where an attacker can intercept and possibly alter the communication between two parties without their knowledge.\n\nIn the context of C++ programming, this vulnerability can occur when a programmer uses libraries or functions that make HTTP requests to unsecured URLs.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, always use HTTPS (HTTP Secure) instead of HTTP when making requests to URLs. HTTPS encrypts the data sent and received, which makes it harder for attackers to intercept or tamper with the data.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nIf you are using the `curl` library to make HTTP requests, you can specify to use HTTPS by simply changing the URL from `http://` to `https://`. Here is an example:\n\n```cpp\n#include <curl/curl.h>\n\nint main(void)\n{\n  CURL *curl;\n  CURLcode res;\n\n  curl_global_init(CURL_GLOBAL_DEFAULT);\n\n  curl = curl_easy_init();\n  if(curl) {\n    curl_easy_setopt(curl, CURLOPT_URL, \"https://yann.lecun.com\");\n\n    /* Perform the request, res will get the return code */ \n    res = curl_easy_perform(curl);\n    /* Check for errors */ \n    if(res != CURLE_OK)\n      fprintf(stderr, \"curl_easy_perform() failed: %s\\n\",\n              curl_easy_strerror(res));\n\n    /* always cleanup */ \n    curl_easy_cleanup(curl);\n  }\n\n  curl_global_cleanup();\n\n  return 0;\n}\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n- libcurl\n\n## References\n\n- [CWE-319: Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/319.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS137138"
                ]
              }
