            {
              "id": "acc65ba0-bf87-3221-9550-ac3dbd2485e5",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is considered a genuine vulnerability because the classification indicates a risk of undefined behavior due to possible overlap between the source and destination memory regions. The analysis detected that the destination and source may overlap based on data flow, which can cause undefined behavior when using memory copy operations like memcpy. Additionally, the verdict for this call site is marked as 'GENUINE', further confirming the risk. The source may also be null, which increases the risk of runtime errors. There are no explicit checks or guards in the code to prevent these issues, and the destination buffer's capacity is not clearly defined or checked. These factors together indicate a real risk that should be addressed.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo prevent undefined behavior when the source and destination memory regions may overlap, use `memmove` instead of `memcpy`. `memmove` is designed to safely handle overlapping memory areas. Replace the original call with:\n\n```cpp\nmemmove(BeginPtr(blob) + bsize, BeginPtr(encode_buf), encode_buf.size());\n```\n\nAdditionally, ensure that both the source and destination pointers are valid and that the destination buffer is large enough to hold the copied data. If the source pointer could be null, add a check before the copy operation:\n\n```cpp\nif (BeginPtr(encode_buf) != nullptr) {\n    memmove(BeginPtr(blob) + bsize, BeginPtr(encode_buf), encode_buf.size());\n}\n```\n\n## References\n- [OWASP: Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n- [C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n\n___\n"
